2026-10-29T22:57:00.8564795Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8576631Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8692724Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8704172Z [0m
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8705643Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8706756Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8707434Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8708028Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8709245Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8709811Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8710349Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8711428Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8711873Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8713368Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8715022Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8716408Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8717343Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8717801Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8718458Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8719157Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8719907Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8721123Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8721761Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8721989Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8722276Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8723359Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8724371Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8725026Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8725346Z I will:
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8725573Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8726066Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8726872Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8727769Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8728567Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8729083Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8729660Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8730319Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8730747Z    /root
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8741779Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8742626Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8757365Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8758347Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8758834Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8763903Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8765005Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8785231Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8785970Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8798147Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8799060Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8799834Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8800203Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8800515Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8800934Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8801403Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8802259Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8802776Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8803284Z If you would like to
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8803939Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8804170Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8804410Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8804804Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8804963Z 
2026-10-29T22:57:00.8804983Z 
